{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1457852-using-predators-with-2e-rules","id":1457852,"title":"Using Predators with 2e rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-27T19:51:20-07:00","id":1457852,"title":"Using Predators with 2e rules","content":"Is there anything, rules-wise I need to convert or keep in mind when using the Spirits in Predators with the 2e WtF ruleset?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T20:15:40-07:00","id":1457856,"title":"","content":"Numina and Manifestations are separate things in 2e, so you may find yourself with room for more Numina than the printed statblock presents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T20:15:57-07:00","id":1457857,"title":"","content":"The Influences + Numina + Manifestations trio of abilities come to mind. Iirc, 1E didn\u2019t have clear-cut borders between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T21:01:04-07:00","id":1457862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1457852-using-predators-with-2e-rules?p=1457857#post1457857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Influences + Numina + Manifestations trio of abilities come to mind. Iirc, 1E didn\u2019t have clear-cut borders between them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are now Manifestations used to just be particular Numina, but Influences were separate from Numina, and one of the things distinguishing ghosts from other spirits was their lack of them (Inferno loosely aligned the ex-ghost Diaboli known as Larvals with historical and folkloric Influences, as a sort of precursor to Influence: Anchors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T22:11:52-07:00","id":1457865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1457852-using-predators-with-2e-rules?p=1457862#post1457862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are now Manifestations used to just be particular Numina, but Influences were separate from Numina, and one of the things distinguishing ghosts from other spirits was their lack of them (Inferno loosely aligned the ex-ghost Diaboli known as Larvals with historical and folkloric Influences, as a sort of precursor to Influence: Anchors).</div> </div> </div> </div>Blast. Knew something was off. <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, Predators. On converting spirits there, you may want to look at the \u201cTwilight Menagerie\u201d thread on the general CofD forum to get a feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-27T23:54:39-07:00","id":1457873,"title":"","content":"Another thing is that spirits in second edition have Banes and Bans, two separate things. This might not be an issue with every spirit, however, cause while they just had Bans in first edition many of them could be used as Banes (objects or other things that might damage the spirit) or Bans (things the spirit couldn't do, or must react in a certain way to). Predators fortunately usually has multiple Bans per spirit and you might find them with one you can just relabel to Bane. And obviously, the unihar isn't a thing anymore.<br /> <br /> In case folks aren't aware, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/2402/Predators\" target=\"_blank\">the PDF of Predators, which has long been unavailable on the DriveThruRPG page, has recently been put back up.</a> It's a really useful book for spirits and some of the other antagonists (though it gets increasingly dated past the Spirits section) and only having it available via hardcopy for years was prohibitive to some, and probably moreso now that the prices on PoD have been hiked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-29T13:00:57-07:00","id":1457992,"title":"","content":"The use of Manifestations are also dependent on appropriate Conditions. For instance, where in First Edition a spirit could use Materialize to take a physical form wherever it pleased, in Second it's necessary to first find a person, place, or object whose nature aligns with the spirit's Influence (the Resonant Condition), then fine tune that state to more closely align with itself either by acting in concert with the subject for a number of scenes or using a Strengthen Influence (the Open Condition). Note that while using an Influence is quicker, it will have a limited duration as Influence uses typically do.<br /> <br /> The same goes for fettering and possession; a spirit can't just attach itself to whatever it pleases, it needs to discriminate based on what fits to it and then spend time or energy preparing it to take the spirit in.<br /> <br /> Claiming is also a bit more of an invested process for spirits; it's necessary to have Possessed a subject on multiple occasions (or used a Control Influence to upgrade the Open Condition) before it is properly conditioned to be a permanent host.<br /> <br /> I don't know the contents of Predators, but I expect these change the dynamics of spirit activity in the material world a decent amount.<br /> <br /> It also introduces a new vulnerability; most of this stuff is dependent on a foundation of being Resonant, so if a subject can be made to no longer be Resonant to the spirit at all then the spirit will often lose its capacity to use the subject to enable Manifestations. A spirit of fire can Fetter itself to a burning building, but loses its grip if the fire is extinguished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 08-29-2021, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}